;; SHIRO & PICO — episode 11 production plan.
;;
;; One file per episode, because loop-ka-production's catalog listing takes the
;; `.edn` basenames in sorted order as the running order, and the loop produces
;; one episode per slot per night. Languages live INSIDE the plan rather than
;; as separate catalog entries: ten catalog ids per episode would make the
;; running order ten nights long for one episode.
;;
;; Every field here is derived from files that already exist in this repo. No
;; title, synopsis or runtime is asserted, because nothing in the repo states
;; them in a machine-readable form and inventing them would put fabricated
;; metadata into the plan the producer trusts.
{:plan/version 1
 :plan/id "episode-11"
 :plan/episode 11
 ;; Counted from the shotlist by row :type. The file has 84 rows total;
 ;; only the "scene" rows are shots, the rest are dialogue lines.
 :plan/shots 23
 :plan/dialogue 61
 :plan/primary-language :en
 :plan/shotlists
 {:ar "episode-11-shotlist-v2.ar.edn"
  :bn "episode-11-shotlist-v2.bn.edn"
  :de "episode-11-shotlist-v2.de.edn"
  :en "episode-11-shotlist-v2.en.edn"
  :es "episode-11-shotlist-v2.es.edn"
  :fr "episode-11-shotlist-v2.fr.edn"
  :hi "episode-11-shotlist-v2.hi.edn"
  :pt "episode-11-shotlist-v2.pt.edn"
  :ta "episode-11-shotlist-v2.ta.edn"
  :zh "episode-11-shotlist-v2.zh.edn"}
 ;; The shotlist is datomize-style tx-data whose attributes are namespaced per
 ;; episode+language (`:shotlist.episode11.en/scene_prompt`). The producer
 ;; derives the namespace from :plan/episode and the language it is rendering,
 ;; rather than each plan repeating it.
 :plan/attr-namespace-template "shotlist.episode%s.%s"}
